{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011zLAQm63o4qaHDkrWxGZHP","type":"tool_result","content":"commit b877c3c502f24c4ad68ae2586d64df1fb19906da\nAuthor: alegomes <alegomes@gmail.com>\nDate:   Thu Oct 8 22:11:48 2026 -0300\n\n    feat(wrap-up): grava o próximo passo do handoff no .next.json (CS-4)\n    \n    O L7 do /common:wrap-up chama o novo common/hooks/session-next.py, que lê\n    a linha **Próximo:** repo=… modo=… comando=… da zona NOTE do handoff e\n    escreve <raiz>/.claude/sessions/<id>.next.json com os três campos e o brief\n    igual ao parágrafo ## Próximo passo, o arquivo que o launcher (CS-3) lê no\n    exit. Sem a linha não escreve e diz; linha inutilizável (repo inexistente,\n    modo desconhecido ou reforma, campo ou brief vazio) não escreve e diz o\n    motivo. O handoff.md documenta a linha.\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n common/commands/handoff.md         |   7 ++\n common/commands/wrap-up.md         |  22 ++++-\n common/hooks/session-next.py       | 124 ++++++++++++++++++++++++\n tests/test_wrapup_proximo_passo.py | 192 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n 4 files changed, 343 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)\ncommon/hooks/modo-escrita-gate.py\ncommon/hooks/_modos.py\ndocs/modos-de-trabalho.md\n-----\n80:  a `/common:spec` specification already closed (one item per success criterion,\n84:  `/common:plan` is the one that writes it. Then `/common:next` names ONE step\n94:- `/common:spec`. Interviews you in rounds until every success criterion has an observable surface and a failing test declared. Writes no code. Resumable.\n156:| `/common:spec` | `<idea in prose> \\| --continuar <slug> \\| --fechar <slug> \\| --lista` | Interviews you in rounds until a high-level idea becomes a buildable specification, recording each answer in a versioned markdown in the repo. Declares it ready only when every success criterion has an observable surface (http/cli/ui/event/domain/application) and a failing test declared on it. Writes no code, needs no Jira (offers Epic + Stories at the end if board-flow is installed). Resumable. |\n157:| `/common:plan` | `<nome> [--from-spec docs/spec/<slug>.md \\| --from-jira [coluna\\|repasse.json]] [--dry-run] [--on-missing refuse\\|keep\\|drop]` | Writes the repo's **single-track execution queue** — `<main-root>/.claude/programs/<nome>/plan.yaml`, the document that keeps the ORDER and the `why` behind each position, which is exactly what a tracker does not keep. Three sources: `--from-spec` turns each success criterion of a `/common:spec` specification into an item, inheriting the order of the text **and saying that it inherited** (a spec's criteria are not prioritised against each other); `--from-jira` writes the queue from a `/board-flow:triage` classification — triage reads the cards, hunts code evidence and proposes the order, and since stage 2 hands it here instead of writing the file itself, so the queue has exactly one writer; with no flag, the queue is dictated by hand — the case of a repo with no tracker and no spec. **No Jira required** for the other two. Writing is mechanical (`common/bin/cepa-plan`): it refuses an empty `why`, a duplicate `id`, a `blocked_by` pointing at a ghost item, a blocking cycle, and — the mirror of `maestro-programs --check-name` — refuses to write the queue over a `parallel-waves` plan. On a rewrite the new list rules the order/title/`why` while the disk keeps `status` and any OPEN `human_pending`, because only the human closes that one. See [execution-plan.md](execution-plan.md). |\n158:| `/common:drain-plan` | `<nome> [--max N] [--dry-run]` | Executes the repo's **single-track queue in the order the queue keeps** — stage 3 of \"one writer, three sources\", closing the trackerless cycle: `/common:plan` writes it, `/common:next` names one step, this one runs several. **No Jira, ever**: the only bulk executor before it, `/board-flow:drain`, takes its order from the board's `priority and rank` — the very order the plan exists to replace. Which items are runnable now is mechanical (`cepa-plan queue`): the batch walks the list from the top and **stops** at the first thing it cannot resolve alone — an open `human_pending` (the owner's call, 2026-08-25), an item blocked by something outside the batch, one already `blocked` by an earlier run, one reserved by another session, or `--max` (default **3**, lower than drain's 5 because each item is a full topology flow plus the acceptance and proof gates). It never skips a stuck item to reach the one below — that is reordering the queue in silence. Each item is reserved before it is touched (`cepa-plan start`) and leaves with a named terminal outcome plus evidence (`cepa-plan finish`, with `--pergunta` carrying the closed question that unblocks a `blocked` item or a new `human_pending`); only the human ever closes a `human_pending`, through `cepa-plan responde`, which refuses without a terminal. Refuses a `parallel-waves` plan — that one is `/maestro:run`'s. See [execution-plan.md](execution-plan.md). |\n3:  \"version\": \"2.26.5\",","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7293735e-1ec8-4108-b1aa-2be184000bb3","uuid":"d394ec7d-9359-4ed3-a610-489e2d50591f","timestamp":"2026-10-09T01:25:05.867Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"commit b877c3c502f24c4ad68ae2586d64df1fb19906da\nAuthor: alegomes <alegomes@gmail.com>\nDate:   Thu Oct 8 22:11:48 2026 -0300\n\n    feat(wrap-up): grava o próximo passo do handoff no .next.json (CS-4)\n    \n    O L7 do /common:wrap-up chama o novo common/hooks/session-next.py, que lê\n    a linha **Próximo:** repo=… modo=… comando=… da zona NOTE do handoff e\n    escreve <raiz>/.claude/sessions/<id>.next.json com os três campos e o brief\n    igual ao parágrafo ## Próximo passo, o arquivo que o launcher (CS-3) lê no\n    exit. Sem a linha não escreve e diz; linha inutilizável (repo inexistente,\n    modo desconhecido ou reforma, campo ou brief vazio) não escreve 